\DOC STRIP_EXISTS_ASSUM_TAC

\TYPE {STRIP_EXISTS_ASSUM_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Finds an existentially quantified assumption, removes it, and replaces it by
its body with the witnesses as free variables and the body's conjuncts as
separate assumptions.

\DESCRIBE
Takes no arguments. Applied to a goal whose assumption list contains an
assumption of the form {?x1 ... xn. t1 /\ ... /\ tk}, the tactic removes that
assumption and puts the conjuncts {t1}, ..., {tk} in its place as individual
assumptions, with {x1 ... xn} now free. The conclusion is untouched. Note that
the removed assumption's position is not preserved: the new assumptions are
appended at the end, while the remaining assumptions keep their relative order.
{
       A, (?x1 ... xn. t1 /\ ... /\ tk) ?- u
       ===================================== STRIP_EXISTS_ASSUM_TAC
       A, t1, ..., tk ?- u
}

\FAILURE
Fails whenever no assumption in the list is an existentially quantified
statement of the shape it can strip; the failure is a search failure raised by
the tactic itself when none of the candidate assumptions is suitable.

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only this one kind of transformation, always on goals
carrying a sizeable assumption list and a conclusion that is not itself
touched.

\ENDDOC
